cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, cite it as below."
title: "ZEPHIRUM — A Computação Antes da Execução"
authors:
  - name: "AUŠRA Quantinum"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SerenaSolutions/zephirum"
abstract: >-
  Certified necessity compiler: answers questions about computations before
  running them. ZEPHIRUM language, ZCA elimination ladder, trivalent logic with
  the numeral Z (zephirum), independent verification. 0 wrong answers in 500,000
  randomized problems; 500,000/500000 certificates verified; 20/20 forged
  certificates rejected; 76.5% of demanded computation units eliminated.
  Phase 3: independent verifier with strict evidence schema, decision
  kernel first-class, SHA-256 certificate hash, entanglement family
  (Schmidt criterion, exact rational arithmetic). Falsification
  experiment: 200 adversarial problems across 4 families
  (boundary equalities, degenerate bounds, 1e16 float traps, lying
  assumptions) with 0 false certificates; 2 engine bugs found and fixed.
keywords:
  - certified computation
  - domain-specific language
  - partial evaluation
  - interval arithmetic
  - proof-carrying certificates
  - trivalent logic
  - computation avoidance
license: MIT
